<title>BRAZIL: Brazil's Cerj shrs up 4 pct on selloff.</title>
<headline>Brazil's Cerj shrs up 4 pct on selloff.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Brazilian power firm Cerj jumped four percent on the Sao Paulo bolsa after a Chilean-led group bought a majority stake in the Rio de Janeiro state company at a privatization auction.</p>
<p>Cerj's ordinary, or voting common, stock rose two centavos to 0.51 reais after the consortium led by Chilectra bought the 70.2-percent stake for 605.3 million reais, brokers said.</p>
<p>The shares closed Tuesday in Sao Paulo at 0.49 reais.</p>
<p>Chilectra is the distribution unit of Chile's Enersis SA.</p>
<p>Other members of the group include Spain's Empresa Nacional de Electricidad, or Endesa, and Portugal's Eletricidade de Portugal (EDP).</p>
<p>-- James Craig, Sao Paulo newsroom 5511 248 5413</p>
